            <div xml:id="d165">

                <pb facs="0327" n="213" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg213"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00R296/5287: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Greece</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Skinner</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Athens</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-11-05T16:00:00+02:00">November 5, 1931—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 5—1:20 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>50. The International Financial Commission informs me that in consequence of
                    information received from the Greek Government, it regards itself as authorized
                    to suspend payment of amounts due <pb facs="0328" n="214" xml:id="pg214"/> the
                    United States on November 10, 1931 and May 10, 1932 in consequence of the
                    applicability of the President’s moratorium program.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Skinner</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
